# Disposal area. Content moved here is dead but deliberately not deleted, so it
# should not be version-tracked. The _* rule below already matches it; this line
# is explicit because _trashcan is disposal, not scratch, and the distinction
# matters when deciding whether something is recoverable. Untracked 2026-07-31;
# the 13 sync-mobile files remain recoverable from commit 0c9fc06.
_trashcan/

# Scratch / unsync conventions inherited from manual phase
_scratch/
**/scratch/
_*
*.scratch.md

# Built plugin packages (output of `zip -r ... writing-cowork.plugin`)
*.plugin

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Editor / OS
*.swp
*~

# Python (when scripts are added under skills/.../scripts/)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Obsidian workspace state (dev repo isn't an Obsidian vault)
.obsidian/

# Accidental Obsidian vault that got created inside the dev repo on 2026-05-19
WritingPlugin/

# Session-close handoffs — ephemeral single-slot baton, never a source of truth.
# Locked 2026-07-23/24; see 1_Project/Decisions.md "Handoff lifecycle".
1_Project/Handoff/
